  #line-at(53.998pt, 413.631pt, "autocorrelation function (Fig. 1b) and optically detected magnetic resonance (ODMR) measurements showing a ")
  #line-at(53.998pt, 430.073pt, "characteristic zero-field resonance at 70 MHz")
  #line-at(251.04pt, 430.08pt, "(Fig. 1c). The other spot is also a single photon emitter (labelled Y) ")
  #line-at(54.022pt, 446.522pt, "without any ODMR peaks in the resonance-frequency range of the V2 center (Fig. 1c). Given the defect creation ")
  #line-at(54.043pt, 462.837pt, "conditions and the detection wavelength range, we attribute defect Y to a single V1 center. This assumption will be ")
  #line-at(54.043pt, 479.279pt, "further justified later by studying the wavelength dependence of the excitation cross-section. In the same region, we ")
