  #line-at(53.998pt, 533.878pt, "is consistent with recent cryogenic measurements by Steidl et al.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(327pt, 530.4pt, "21")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(333.96pt, 533.88pt, ", which attributed the observed optical-resonance ")
  #line-at(54.004pt, 550.322pt, "instability of V2 centers to charge fluctuations likely originating from nearby carbon vacancies. ")
  #line-at(54.004pt, 583.079pt, "Based on the extracted ionization cross-sections (Fig. 3d), the V2 center is expected to be inherently less susceptible ")
  #line-at(54.014pt, 599.521pt, "to photoionization than the V1 center under resonant excitation because of its longer ZPL wavelength. These findings ")
  #line-at(54.014pt, 615.836pt, "are directly connected to higher charge stability, highlighting the advantage of V2 for spin–photon interface ")
  #line-at(54.025pt, 632.278pt, "applications. In addition, the rapidly increasing background ionization at shorter wavelengths (Fig. 4a left) can limit ")
  #line-at(54.014pt, 648.72pt, "spectral stability, particularly for V1, whereas it remains weaker near the V2 ZPL. Although a qualitative trend is ")
  #line-at(54.015pt, 665.035pt, "anticipated from the general expectation that shorter-wavelength excitation enhances ionization, neither the ionization ")
  #line-at(54.015pt, 681.477pt, "cross-sections of individual V1 and V2 centers nor the wavelength dependence of their surrounding charge ")
  #line-at(54.015pt, 697.919pt, "environment had been quantitatively established prior to this work. ")
  #line-at(54.015pt, 730.676pt, "In addition, the pronounced ionization of background defects, primarily carbon vacancies, provides important insight ")
  #line-at(54.025pt, 747.118pt, "into how repump or off-resonant excitation can modify the local charge environment, complementing earlier ")
  #line-at(54.025pt, 763.433pt, "cryogenic observations of resonance fluctuations under resonant excitation.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.64pt, 759.96pt, "21")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(381.6pt, 763.44pt, " These insights provide a quantitative ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 413.64pt, "Figure 4. V2 center photocurrent fraction (PCF) analysis for PDMR applications. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(410.884pt, 413.64pt, "a")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(416.041pt, 413.64pt, " Left: Excitation-wavelength ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 429.96pt, "dependence of the background measured around defect X; Right: The wavelength dependence of the PCF defined ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 446.4pt, "by V2/(V2+BG). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(130.56pt, 446.4pt, "b")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.56pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(136.442pt, 446.4pt, " The wavelength dependence of the PCFs. Left: V2/(V2+V1); Right; V2/(V2+V1+BG). All PCF ")
  #line-at(56.64pt, 462.84pt, "values are estimated by interpolating the experimental laser-power-dependent measurement results in Fig. 3b. ")
]

